{"abstract":[{"text":"Kellner (Herbert Anton Kellner, 1977).","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kellner","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Five fifths — C→G, G→D, D→A, A→E, and B→F♯ — are each narrowed by ⅕ of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Pythagorean comma, equal to ⁵√(2¹⁴\/3⁷) ≈ 697.654 cents. The remaining seven","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fifths are pure (3:2). The circle closes exactly.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Proposed by Kellner as a reconstruction of Bach’s own tuning, published in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Das Musikinstrument","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" 26 (1977). The choice of five fifths and their positions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mirrors the structure of Werckmeister III while spreading the tempering more evenly.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament\/kellner"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/